# local daemon state
# The -wal/-shm sidecars are NOT matched by *.db, and sqlite writes all three:
# a watcher started without QOOQ_WATCHER_SQLITE_PATH puts its database in the
# current directory, so running one from a checkout drops the set here.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# compose secrets (QOOQ_TOKEN etc.) — never commit
# The patterns are deliberately wider than `.env`: a timestamped backup of a
# filled-in env file holds the same live secrets the original does, and a bare
# `.env` rule does not cover it. Example files are the one thing that is meant
# to be committed, so they are excepted by name.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example

# watcher / daemon config written by hand on a machine — these hold qooqd.token,
# secret.key and git credentials, so they are the same class of thing as .env.
# Anchored to the paths the watcher actually reads (./config.* and
# ./configs/config.*): an unanchored `config.toml` also matches
# examples/config-file-app/config.toml, and then a new example carrying one is
# silently skipped by `git add -A`.
/config.toml
/config.yaml
/config.yml
/configs/config.*

# private keys (GitHub App, SSH). Never needed in a checkout: pkg/buildctx.TarDir
# only excludes .git, so a key left here also travels into a docker build context.
*.pem

# built binaries
/qooq
/qooqd
/bin/

# editor/OS noise
.DS_Store

# goreleaser 產物
dist/

# 本機測試用的破壞性腳本
/scratch/
.shapes-cache/

# AI 開發筆記（給 Claude Code 等 agent 讀的本機檔，不進公開 repo）
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
